25 demand and before our October 27 reply; used for substance only, no inference drawn about who participated). Their package: the four invoices at 265,200 over six months, $0 on J-4533, $0 conversion fees, mutual release, each side bears its own fees. Strictly valued (the note states no interest): 265,200 - exactly the conceded principal with all accrued Section 2 interest waived (276,417.47 - 265,200 = 11,217.47 at October 25; 277,920.27 - 265,200 = 12,720.27 at the filing basis) and 44,720.27 below the walk-away (309,920.27 - 265,200.00), before any further discount for the six-month payout. On an assumed schedule of six equal monthly installments of 44,200 with Section 2 continuing at 1%/month on unpaid balances (ASSUMPTION, not their stated terms - interest treatment and schedule are unknown; Q11 asked), the block would pay 265,200 + 9,282.00 (1% x 44,200 x 21) = 274,482.00 by month six, still 3,438.27 below the filing-basis floor and 35,438.27 below the walk-away. Recommendation on the arithmetic: reject as stated, hold the November 11 AAA filing, counter only at or above the walk-away; the one aligned term (mutual release, each side bears its own fees) is offered by them in their own words and matches our default because neither side's lawyer bill exists in any record we hold. FEE EXPOSURE. The numeric field is 0 and means NOT QUANTIFIED - NOT known to be zero: Exhibit C.3 is mutual (recovery for us if we prevail; their fee claim on any segment we lose, worst case the conversions, where implied-waiver/estoppel exposure rests on the Bell-Lindqvist texts and a roughly six-minute May call of unknown content); opposing counsel themselves invoked C.3 on the October 20 call, against an interference claim that was dropped before the demand and stays dropped; no rate or time data exists for either side's fees; AAA administration costs are unverified (schedule not in the library). STANDING RULES. Every payment stops Section 2 interest at receipt; no interest is ever claimed on conversion fees; the February 11 written waiver for Rosa M. and Tay W. stands untouched; dropped theories (tortious interference, the seven-hire 112,000, any court filing, the 862,000 target) stay out of every scenario."
}

